AB  - Breathing polluted air can cause severe health impacts, which might be irreversible in many cases. However, these issues can be tackled with the existing and improving technologies, which can help the government keep track of the air pollution issue to take proactive measures. We have observed that the influence of the neural network, machine learning model, and variants have rapidly risen in almost every sector. Air pollution is also one of them. However, the pre-existing models struggle to capture the accurate relationship between the variables and the result, thereby giving biased results or predictions. Hence in this study, we have comprehensively scrutinized several robust studies covering the models relating to the neural network, regression, and hybrid models in the field of air pollution. We have comprehensively surveyed the application and implementation of the neural network, regression, and hybrid models and techniques in air pollution and summarised several studies in a tabular format for ease of understanding. This study provides the much-needed information and will play a vital role in competing for safety considerations and mitigating the air pollution issue by predicting the Air Quality Index and air pollutant concentration.
