AB  - Air pollution affects the national economy and social development. PM2.5 (particulate matter with an aerodynamic diameter of less than 2.5 mu m) is one of the major pollutants. The accurate and timely prediction of its concentration is significant to preventing and controlling air pollution. This study proposed a prediction model combining fast Fourier transform and long and short-term memory neural network (FFT-LSTM) for eliminating the effect of spatial-temporal heterogeneity of air pollutants and meteorological elements and achieving longtime prediction. The model extracts the best common period of each element based on FFT as the model input takes the PM2.5 concentration in the future 24 h as the model output. We established a double temporal sliding block to make the model capture the long-term change rule of the time series of each variable through time sliding and achieve high accuracy and long-term prediction. According to the regional rule of the best common period of each element, we refined the division of Hebei Province in China and established models suitable for different regions. The prediction accuracy of this model was compared with traditional LSTM and long short-Term memory extended (LSTME) models. The results showed that the performance of the FFT-LSTM model is better than that of other models. In addition, we tested the model's applicability for the prediction of other pollutants such as PM10 and SO2. This model effectively improves the prediction accuracy of air pollutants, which can provide technical reference for air quality early warning.
