AB  - Aiming at the problems that traditional air pollutant prediction models cannot meet the needs of intelligent processing of big data, and the processing effect is not ideal. A pollutant diffusion trend prediction model using deep learning in air quality monitoring big data is proposed. Firstly, the air pollutant data are preprocessed such as data cleaning, and the data features that can be used for prediction are selected by grey correlation analysis. Then, based on the deep belief network (DBN) learning and analyzing the data feature set, in order to realize the prediction of the diffusion trend of air pollutants. Finally, the two processes of pre-training of unsupervised learning and model parameter tuning of supervised learning are combined. Continuously fine-tune the parameters of the DBN model until the best predictive model structure is obtained. The proposed model is demonstrated experimentally based on the MATA-LAB simulation platform. The results show that the predicted value is very close to the actual value. Taking June as an example, the forecast result is the most accurate, and the highest root mean square error does not exceed 11.5, which has certain practical application value.
