AB  - SO2 and PM10 are among the air pollutants that play the most effective role in air pollution. In the study, estimates were made in 2020 that these contaminants were affected by the Covid-19 pandemic using recurrent artificial neural networks, one of the deep learning approaches that are very popular today. Data belonging to Sakarya province, where industrialization is concentrated, was obtained from the air monitoring center of the Ministry of Environment and Urbanization, and modeling and optimization was carried out in Python software. The statistical analysis of the obtained SO2 and PM10 estimation results was made and when compared with the actual data, values of 0.67-0.88 in correlation and 2.84-14.09 in RMSE were reached. The results were compared with other studies in the related literature and showed how well deep learning architectures can yield under conditions that negatively affect prediction techniques such as Covid-19. In addition, it has been observed that the PM10 value for Sakarya province exceeds the legal limit three times on some days, especially during peak production periods.
